# Files that run or are read on a Linux server must keep LF line endings, even in a checkout made
# on Windows with core.autocrlf=true. A CRLF shell script fails with
#   /usr/bin/env: 'bash\r': No such file or directory
# and a CRLF systemd unit, nginx config or sudoers file can fail to parse or mis-read a value.
# Scoped deliberately to these types: a repo-wide `* text=auto` would renormalise every file.
*.sh        text eol=lf
*.service   text eol=lf
*.conf      text eol=lf
*.sudoers   text eol=lf
deploy/**   text eol=lf
